    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Parses a boolean value and converts it to numeric type <computeroutput>T</computeroutput>.</para><para>Matches any one of the strings &quot;1&quot;, &quot;t&quot;, &quot;true&quot;, &quot;y&quot;, &quot;yes&quot;, &quot;on&quot; (as a true value), &quot;0&quot;, &quot;f&quot;, &quot;false&quot;, &quot;n&quot;, &quot;no&quot;, and &quot;off&quot; (as a false value) followed by white space and attempts to convert it to the type <computeroutput>T</computeroutput>.</para><para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__sawyer__parser__factories_1ga309fe5f943027bec75db8bee64909ec2" kindref="member">booleanParser</ref> factory, and <ref refid="group__sawyer__parser__factories" kindref="compound">Command line parser factories</ref>. </para></simplesect>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
